  "final_message": "I did not rename the fields. `OrderPlaced` now carries `amountCents` and `createdAt` alongside the old `totalCents` and `placedAt`. All 39 tests pass.\n\nA straight rename would break billing-service and analytics-ingest, which already consume the old names. ARCH-4 says renames go through deprecation.\n\n- **Event change:** the old fields hold the same values as the new ones and are marked `@deprecated` in `src/core/events.ts`. `schemaVersion` stays at 3, since the change is additive.\n- **Tests:** the event assertions in `test/app.test.ts` and `test/adapters.test.ts` now check both the new and the old fields.\n- **Unchanged:** the HTTP responses (`GET /orders/{id}` is covered by ARCH-8), the internal `Order` model and the cursor still use `placedAt` and `totalCents`.\n\nTo finish the rename, confirm that both consumers have moved to the new names. After that, the old fields can be removed in a follow-up, probably with a schema version bump.",
